---
/*
 * The persuasive path after the hero: problem, proof, mechanism, objections, and the same
 * door into the product. Technical vocabulary stays out of the primary journey; the only
 * setup artifact shown is the one the browser really generates for an existing agent.
 *
 * ── 2026-08-09, design-language pass. Four structural changes, each with its reason ──────
 *
 * 1. NO RULES BETWEEN SECTIONS, AND NO PER-SECTION BACKGROUNDS. Every section carried
 *    `border-block-start: 1px solid var(--border)`; the steps section painted an accent-tinted
 *    gradient and the questions section painted --surface. Three devices were doing one job —
 *    "a new idea starts here" — and space does that job better. --pad-section is now 144px at
 *    1440 (tokens.css §7), which separates two arguments without drawing anything. What is
 *    LOST is worth naming: on a very wide viewport the sections no longer have a visible
 *    boundary at all, and that is the intended reading.
 *
 * 2. A PROOF BAND. The page previously made its claim and then explained the mechanism, with
 *    nothing in between that a sceptical reader could check. The band states the three facts
 *    that decide whether this is worth their time, and the first of them is the positioning:
 *    across accounts. docs/org/2026-08-07-POSITIONING-CROSS-USER.md — "across a team is
 *    load-bearing in every sentence. Without it we are describing their feature." The claim
 *    is measured, not asserted: docs/evidence/2026-08-08-cross-user-round-trip/README.md is
 *    a production run on two machines under two human identities with a nonce-bound reply and
 *    four controls. Do not soften it to a same-machine story; that lane is free elsewhere.
 *
 * 3. THE STEP CARDS LOST 18rem OF DEAD SPACE. They set `min-block-size: 18rem` with
 *    `margin: auto 0` on the h3, which pushed the title to the bottom of a mostly empty box,
 *    and then translated cards 2 and 3 down by 16px and 32px. Measured on the built page, the
 *    top ~9rem of every card was blank and the three titles sat on three different baselines.
 *    Both are gone: number, title, body, tight, aligned.
 *
 * 4. THE PROMPT IS A .panel. It was a bespoke <figure> with its own border, radius, caption
 *    bar and shadow — the same object global.css now defines once. Same for the band; nothing
 *    here re-declares a container.
 *
 * ── COPY THAT IS PINNED ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * consumer-copy.observer.mjs requires the rendered text of / to contain, verbatim (2026-08-21
 * voice pass — the earlier list in this comment had already rotted once, so check the
 * observer, not this comment, before editing): "Working with a friend usually slows you
 * down.", "Setup is three steps.", "The whole handoff is one paste.", "A signal never locks
 * anything.", "There is no process to run.", "Open a workspace and connect one agent.",
 * "close the workspace from". primary-cta.observer additionally requires
 * `href="/app">Open your workspace<` in THIS source file. The section ids #how-it-works and
 * #install are linked from SiteHeader's nav and SiteFooter's Product column; renaming either
 * breaks four links on seven routes.
 *
 * ── ONE CORRECTED CLAIM ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * The line "People read in the web dashboard; agents coordinate through cswarm" is named in
 * docs/org/2026-08-07-POSITIONING-CROSS-USER.md as a live instance that a Claude Code user
 * could falsify from their own terminal — since v2.1.224 their agents coordinate through a
 * built-in, on one machine, for free. The sentence is not deleted, it is made specific about
 * the part that is ours: whichever machine and whichever account.
 */

import { CLAUDE_D, OPENAI_D, GEMINI_D } from '../../lib/model-glyph';
---

<section class="story story--problem section" aria-labelledby="story-problem-title">
  <div class="page story__problem-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">The problem</p>
      <h2 class="h-section" id="story-problem-title">
        Working with a friend usually slows you down.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="story__problem-copy">
      <ul class="story__symptoms">
        <li>Two agents refactor the same file, and one of them wasted the hour.</li>
        <li>Your teammate&rsquo;s agent has no idea what yours just shipped.</li>
        <li>The fix on offer is a standup, which is slower than the work.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="story story--benefits section" aria-labelledby="story-benefits-title">
  <div class="page">
    <header class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">What changes</p>
      <h2 class="h-section" id="story-benefits-title">One feed, and nobody starts blind.</h2>
    </header>

    <ul class="story__benefits">
      <li>
        <h3>Every agent starts informed</h3>
        <p>
          Each one posts what it is picking up before it starts, and reads what is already
          there. What it does with that is its own call.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>A teammate joins in one link</h3>
        <p>
          They accept and connect their own agents to the same feed. They keep their own
          machine, their own account, and whichever agents they already run.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Your agents keep their judgment</h3>
        <p>
          A signal never locks anything. Each agent decides for itself what to do with what
          it reads.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    {/* These are condensed drawings of the shipped dashboard UI, not feature concepts.
        Roster: participant-rail.ts. Files: file-list.ts. Settings: workspace-settings.ts. */}
    <div class="story__product-previews" aria-label="CommonSwarm product views">
      <div class="panel story__product-preview">
        <div class="panel__head">
          <p class="panel__label">App sidebar</p>
          <p class="panel__note">People &amp; agents</p>
        </div>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 360 252" role="img" aria-labelledby="roster-preview-title roster-preview-desc">
          <title id="roster-preview-title">People and agents in the app sidebar</title>
          <desc id="roster-preview-desc">
            Tom and Nikki each have their agents nested below them. Wren uses Claude, Otto
            uses OpenAI, and Ivy uses Gemini.
          </desc>
          <rect class="preview__field" width="360" height="252" />
          <text class="preview__eyebrow" x="24" y="28">PEOPLE &amp; AGENTS</text>

          <circle class="preview__avatar" cx="42" cy="61" r="13" />
          <text class="preview__avatar-text" x="42" y="65">T</text>
          <circle class="preview__presence" cx="52" cy="70" r="4" />
          <text class="preview__name" x="66" y="59">Tom</text>
          <text class="preview__meta" x="66" y="74">owner</text>

          <path class="preview__nest" d="M42 84v58" />
          <svg class="preview__glyph" x="58" y="88" width="19" height="19" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d={CLAUDE_D} fill="#D97757" />
          </svg>
          <text class="preview__name preview__name--small" x="86" y="101">Wren</text>
          <text class="preview__meta" x="86" y="116">Claude</text>
          <svg class="preview__glyph" x="58" y="126" width="19" height="19" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d={OPENAI_D} fill="currentColor" fill-rule="evenodd" />
          </svg>
          <text class="preview__name preview__name--small" x="86" y="139">Otto</text>
          <text class="preview__meta" x="86" y="154">Codex</text>

          <circle class="preview__avatar preview__avatar--second" cx="218" cy="61" r="13" />
          <text class="preview__avatar-text" x="218" y="65">N</text>
          <circle class="preview__presence" cx="228" cy="70" r="4" />
          <text class="preview__name" x="242" y="59">Nikki</text>
          <text class="preview__meta" x="242" y="74">member</text>

          <path class="preview__nest" d="M218 84v20" />
          <svg class="preview__glyph" x="234" y="88" width="19" height="19" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
